  <p class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">StackGeist</a> / <a href="/gear">Gear</a> / <a href="/gear/budget-tech">Budget tech</a> / <a href="/gear/budget-tech/compare">Compare</a> / GaN station vs wall brick</p>
  <p class="page-kicker">Head to head</p>
  <h1 class="page-title">Multi-Port GaN Station vs Single Wall Brick</h1>
  <p class="page-lead">A 500W multi-port GaN station replaces a pile of separate bricks with one desktop unit. A single 100W wall brick is smaller, cheaper, and dead simple. The right answer depends entirely on how many devices you charge at your desk vs how many rooms you charge across.</p>

  <section class="content-section">
    <table class="cmp">
      <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>500W Multi-Port GaN Station</th><th>Single 100W Wall Brick</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody><tr><td>Total output</td><td>300-500W (across all ports)</td><td>65W - 140W (single device)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ports</td><td>4-8 mixed USB-C + USB-A</td><td>1 USB-C</td></tr>
<tr><td>Footprint</td><td>Palm-sized brick with cable</td><td>Wall plug the size of a matchbox</td></tr>
<tr><td>Outlets used</td><td>1</td><td>1 per device</td></tr>
<tr><td>Best for</td><td>Desks with 3+ devices</td><td>Single laptop or single device</td></tr>
<tr><td>Price range</td><td>$80-150</td><td>$25-60</td></tr>
<tr><td>Portability</td><td>Backpack-friendly but bulky</td><td>Pocket / bag</td></tr>
<tr><td>Heat under load</td><td>Warm to hot</td><td>Warm</td></tr></tbody>
    </table>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">When 500W Multi-Port GaN Station wins</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Pick 500W Multi-Port GaN Station if...</h2>
    <p>Your desk has 3+ chargers on it right now. A laptop, a phone, headphones, an iPad, a Switch — every device came with its own brick and every brick eats an outlet. One GaN station consolidates all of them into one wall plug.</p><p>You share a workspace with a partner or roommate. Two people, two laptops, two phones, one shared station is easier than negotiating outlet space.</p><p>You travel and want to carry one charger for everything instead of a laptop brick + phone brick + headphones dongle. Weight goes down, packing gets simpler.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">When Single 100W Wall Brick wins</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Pick Single 100W Wall Brick if...</h2>
    <p>You only have one laptop and everything else uses wireless charging or lives in another room. Buying a 500W station for a single-device setup is spending $100 to do the job of a $40 brick.</p><p>You want the smallest possible travel charger. A single 100W GaN wall brick fits in a pocket. Multi-port stations don't.</p><p>You want charging that follows you from room to room. Wall bricks live in different outlets. A desktop station is stuck at the desk.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <p class="page-kicker">The verdict</p>
    <p>Count the chargers currently on your desk. Three or more, buy the station. Fewer, buy a good single wall brick.</p><p>The station's value is not raw wattage. It's outlets-consolidated and cable-management-improved. If those aren't problems for you, a $40 100W GaN wall brick is the right buy and half the cost.</p>
  </section>

